{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible light-induced, copper-catalyzed aerobic oxidation of terminal alkynes to glyoxals, which are then converted into \u03b1-keto esters, quinoxalines, and naphthoquinones. The method uses inexpensive CuI as a catalyst, 2-picolinic acid as a ligand, and molecular oxygen as the oxidant, avoiding over-oxidation and homocoupling byproducts. Key findings include high functional group tolerance, compatibility with primary, secondary, and tertiary alcohols, and the successful synthesis of biologically active molecules like CFTR activators and DHPS inhibitors.",
